From: SophiaWJ <jingwangsophia@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 03:24:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] gpui_apple: drop a replaced surface hook outside the
 lock, re-export gpu_surfaces from gpui_macos

Review fixes for the surface reports:

- set_hook drops the hook it replaces with the lock released, so what the
  old hook captured may use the hook functions as it drops. A new test
  deadlocked on the old set_hook and passes now.
- A hook test that fails keeps the hook's test lock, so the next hook test
  now gives up after 30 s instead of hanging the test binary.
- The Hook doc says it must not panic: Completed is delivered from an
  Objective-C block.
- gpui_macos::metal_renderer re-exports gpu_surfaces beside the renderer's
  other items, so a gpui user can reach it; the paint_surface and
  SurfaceSource docs point there and name both accepted formats.
- parking_lot::RwLock, as the rest of the crate.

Release Notes:

- N/A
